  "title": "amnoise",
  "description": "This dataset contains magnetoencephalography (MEG) recordings from a single infant subject participating in a study of auditory processing and phoneme learning, part of research investigating risk factors for dyslexia during sensitive periods of language development. The data support investigations into neural theta sampling and auditory deficits in infants at risk for dyslexia.",
  "methods_description": "MEG data were collected from an infant subject and converted to BIDS format using MNE-BIDS. The dataset includes magnetoencephalographic recordings acquired during auditory and linguistic tasks.",
